      "passageHtml": "<div class=\"source-doc chat-doc\"><p><strong>Gary Wendel (7:40 A.M.)</strong><br>Good morning, team. Can you share the current status of your projects, please?</p>\n<p><strong>Jing Yu (7:42 A.M.)</strong><br>I met with the client last week to confirm the start date for Phase B of the Palisade project.</p>\n<p><strong>Robbie Zuniga (7:43 A.M.)</strong><br>I am headed to the job site now for the Riverview project. The rain last week delayed pouring the concrete for the sidewalks. I will check the conditions this morning to see if the situation has improved.</p>\n<p><strong>Gary Wendel (7:44 A.M.)</strong><br>When will Phase B of the Palisade project begin?</p>\n<p><strong>Jing Yu (7:46 A.M.)</strong><br>We will break ground in March and plan to have the building completed by November.</p>\n<p><strong>Gary Wendel (7:47 A.M.)</strong><br>That’s good news about the March start date. I am sure the client is happy about that.</p>\n<p><strong>Gary Wendel (7:50 A.M.)</strong><br>Robbie, let me know what you find out about the site conditions. Perhaps Nathan Burry can help at the site. He’s our most knowledgeable concrete finisher.</p>\n<p><strong>Robbie Zuniga (7:55 A.M.)</strong><br>Actually, I’m meeting Nathan at the site this morning, so I’ll get his opinion on when we can pour the concrete. The rest of the project is on hold until we can do this.</p>\n<p><strong>Gary Wendel (7:57 A.M.)</strong><br>Keep me posted. I don’t want to rush it if it’s still too wet. At the same time, the Riverview project is already behind schedule because of equipment problems and late delivery of building materials.</p>\n<p><strong>Robbie Zuniga (7:58 A.M.)</strong><br>Will do.</p></div>",
